1
00:05:11,250 --> 00:05:17,250
Code name, D-Day, June 6th 1944

2
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:28,500
Overlord is a drama, history, war film directed by Stuart Cooper.

3
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:39,750
During World War II, a young man is called up and, with an increasing sense of
foreboding, undertakes his army training ready for D-Day, June 6th, 1944.

4
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Tom, played by Brian Stirner.

5
00:25:56,250 --> 00:26:02,250
Jack, played by Davyd Harries.

6
00:31:07,500 --> 00:31:13,500
Arthur, played by Nicholas Ball.

7
00:36:18,750 --> 00:36:24,750
The Girl, played by Julie Neesam.

8
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:36,000
The Trained Soldier, played by Sam Sewell.

9
00:46:41,250 --> 00:46:47,250
Dad, played by John Franklyn-Robbins.

10
00:51:52,500 --> 00:51:58,500
Overlord is a 1975 black-and-white British war film
written and directed by Stuart Cooper.

11
00:57:03,750 --> 00:57:09,750
Set during the Second World War, around the D-Day invasion (Operation Overlord), the film is about a young British
soldier's experiences and his meditations on being part of the war machinery, including his premonitions of death.

12
01:02:15,000 --> 01:02:21,000
The film won the Silver Bear - Special Jury Prize at the
25th Berlin International Film Festival.

13
01:07:26,250 --> 01:07:32,250
“Overlord is not about military heroics; on the contrary, it is
about the bleakness of sacrifice”, Cooper said.

14
01:12:37,500 --> 01:12:43,500
The film explores themes of world war ii, d-day, black and white, london blitz.

15
01:17:48,750 --> 01:17:54,750
The tone is emotional.
